# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in your key.
# `.env` is git-ignored - NEVER commit your real key.

# Required. Get a free key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Optional. Current free-tier-friendly models include gemini-3.5-flash,
# gemini-3.6-flash, gemini-3.7-flash, gemini-3.8-flash, gemini-3.1-flash-lite.
# The older 2.x generation (gemini-2.5-flash etc.) is no longer available to
# new API keys - if you see a 404 mentioning that, switch to one of the above.
#
# NOTE ON DAILY QUOTA: the gemini-3.x-flash variants (3.5/3.6/3.7/3.8) share
# the same small free-tier cap - 20 requests/day EACH, confirmed via
# https://aistudio.google.com/rate-limit, which is easy to exhaust while
# actively developing (every retry counts as a separate request). If you're
# hitting 429s often during development, gemini-3.1-flash-lite is worth
# switching to - it carries a much larger free-tier daily allowance (500/day,
# seen directly on the same dashboard) on top of being a separate quota bucket
# from the -flash models above, so it isn't affected by having exhausted those.
# Check your own real-time usage at https://aistudio.google.com/rate-limit
# (requires login) - the "requests per day" column there is a 28-day PEAK
# usage chart, not a live "remaining today" countdown, so a number showing
# above the model's limit means some past day went over, not that you're
# necessarily blocked right now.
# Defaults to gemini-3.5-flash if unset.
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.5-flash

# Optional. Per-request timeout in MILLISECONDS. Defaults to 90000 (90s).
# Gemini's 3.x models do internal "thinking" before answering, so this app's
# planning call (long prompt + large JSON schema) can take much longer than a
# simple chat message. A too-short timeout here doesn't just fail faster - it
# can cut generation off mid-response and come back as a technically valid but
# EMPTY plan, which is more confusing than a clean timeout error.
# GEMINI_TIMEOUT_MS=90000

# Optional. How much internal reasoning Gemini 3.x does before answering:
# "minimal", "low", "medium", or "high". NOT set to the floor ("minimal") -
# that was tried and made things worse: with zero thinking, a smaller model
# (gemini-3.1-flash-lite) fell into a genuine repetition loop and never
# finished the JSON at all. A little reasoning is what stops that. Less
# "thinking" is not free, especially for a small/fast model.
# Defaults to "low".
# GEMINI_THINKING_LEVEL=low

# Optional. Output token budget per call. Needs to be generous enough for a
# full multi-step plan to complete without being cut off - an earlier default
# of 8192 still wasn't always enough. Defaults to 16384.
# GEMINI_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS=16384

# Optional. Set to "false" to skip the second-pass LLM crisis check and save
# quota. The free keyword-based crisis check always runs regardless.
# ENABLE_LLM_CRISIS_CHECK=true
